---
description: Web app UI conventions, shadcn components and AI Elements
globs: apps/web/**, packages/ui/**
alwaysApply: false
---

- Prefer existing components over custom UI. Check, in order:
  1. Components already in `packages/ui/src/components` (shadcn parts and
     domain-free AI Element patterns such as Task, Suggestion, Terminal).
  2. shadcn components: https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components.md
  3. AI Elements patterns for agent UI (chat, reasoning, tool calls, plan,
     task, terminal, test results, file tree, subagent and more):
     https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/ai-elements.md
- Write custom UI only when none of these fit, and build it from them.
- Add a shadcn component from the repo root:
  `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name> -c apps/web`. The `ui` alias puts it
  in `packages/ui/src/components`. Import it as
  `@workspace/ui/components/<name>`. Some items also add hooks or libs
  under `apps/web/src`. Preview with `--dry-run` first. Do not hand-copy
  component code.
- AI Elements: add the base components they build on (e.g.
  `pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add trace code-block -c apps/web`), then copy
  the Base UI pattern from
  `https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/ai-elements/base/<pattern>.md` into
  `packages/ui/src/components/` when it stays domain-free. Patterns that
  bind `@workspace/shared` (e.g. `ModelSelector`) stay in
  `apps/web/src/components/ai-elements/`.
- This project uses Base UI (style `base-nova`), not Radix. Use the Base UI
  variant of docs and examples.
- Style with Tailwind 4 and the theme tokens in
  `packages/ui/src/styles/globals.css`. Use `cn()` from
  `@workspace/ui/lib/utils`.
- Call the API only through the typed client in `src/lib/api.ts`
  (`hc<AppType>`). Never hardcode the server URL; Vite proxies `/api`.
- Add `data-testid` to elements that e2e tests assert on.
- UI changes need a Playwright test in `apps/e2e`, and the PR includes its
  video and screenshots.
